{"id": 8606, "name": "Tetsa River Regional Park", "read": "2026-10-15", "pages": [{"url": "https://www.northernrockies.ca/community-recreation/camping-parks-facilities/tetsa-river-regional-park-campground", "lines": ["hiking, biking and horseback riding. Don’t forget your camera! | Tetsa River Regional Campground is located a few kilometres south of Tetsa River Lodge and has 25 unserviced campsites that may be reserved in advance for $20/night including tax and firewood, online or by contacting the Northern Rockies Regional Recreation Centre at 250.774.2541 option 1. It is a popular location for locals on the weekend due to its pr"]}, {"url": "https://www.northernrockies.ca/resident-services", "lines": [], "via": "Resident Services"}, {"url": "https://www.northernrockies.ca/resident-services/community-services-directory", "lines": ["ccess to barrier-free, non-judgmental, confidential support and follow-up to youth, adults, and seniors through 24/7 phone lines and online services. | BC Housing | Type(s) Affordable Housing If your household income is $35,000.00 or less, you may be eligible to receive cash assistance with your monthly rent payments. | BC Hydro | Type(s) Utilities Electricity services. | BC Suicide Line | Type(s) Mental Health 1-800", ", Transportation If you are calling from outside British Columbia please call 1.250.564.7499. | Travel service program for patients needing out-of-town medical appointments in northern BC. Fares are nominal ranging from $20.00 round-trip to $80.00 round trip for longer distance routes. | Northern Lamplighters Senior Activity Centre | Type(s) Seniors Is a non-profit organization for seniors, organizing senior recreati", "ncludes a main, side, fresh fruit cup, homemade dinner bun and a dessert. They have volunteers who deliver for them or pick up is an option as well. The Northern Rockies Seniors Bus is now available to everyone! In town $5.00/day and out of town: $10.00/day. | Northern Rockies Senior Society - Meals on Wheels | Type(s) Food Resources The Meals on Wheels program offers a hot homemade meal to seniors within our communi", " | Northern Rockies Senior Society - Meals on Wheels | Type(s) Food Resources The Meals on Wheels program offers a hot homemade meal to seniors within our community, twice weekly, Tuesday and Thursday for a small fee of $10/meal. This meal includes a main, side, fresh fruit cup, homemade dinner bun and a dessert. They have volunteers who deliver for them or pick up is always an option as well. | Northern Rockies Seni", "ecializing in seniors and people with mobility issue transportation. The bus is equipped with a wheelchair lift and can take up to 5 wheelchairs at a time. | Operating Tuesday - Friday, 10AM - 2PM, with in town rates of $10.00 per day (capped at 5 trips) and out of town rates of $15.00 per day (With pick up and return to point of origin or final destination and up to 3 pick up around town), and a one way Airport Fee ", "in town rates of $10.00 per day (capped at 5 trips) and out of town rates of $15.00 per day (With pick up and return to point of origin or final destination and up to 3 pick up around town), and a one way Airport Fee of $20. Please visit their website to view all limits and restrictions. | Bus passes are available from either the driver or the office. | If you would like to advertise your business on the outside of t"], "via": "Community Services Directory"}, {"url": "https://www.northernrockies.ca/resident-services/garbage-recycling", "lines": ["m or snowbank and without obstacles or snow build-up. | Landfill and Landfill Hours | 3100 55th Street, Fort Nelson | P: 250.774.7194 | A typical residential load, such as the back of a pickup, is charged a flat rate of $5. Commercial loads are a flat rate of $10. Qualifying large appliances are now accepted free of charge through NRRM’s partnership with MARR. Learn more in Recycling - Large Appliance Recycling. | Pl"], "via": "Garbage and Recycling"}, {"url": "https://www.northernrockies.ca/resident-services/garbage-recycling/kitchen-soil-commercial-organics-diversion-pilot", "lines": [], "via": "Kitchen to Soil - Commercial Organics Diversion Pilot"}]}
